00:12:26,280 --> 00:12:29,221
The needle's still pointing
toward Fishman Island.

260
00:12:29,340 --> 00:12:32,757
Let's just hope that this island
isn't going to rewrite the log on us.

261
00:12:32,840 --> 00:12:34,220
You. It's fine.

262
00:12:34,320 --> 00:12:36,597
The Savoote Archipelago is
just a cluster of trees.

263
00:12:36,680 --> 00:12:37,957
There's no magnetic field.

264
00:12:38,040 --> 00:12:39,697
It's not actually a real island.

265
00:12:39,780 --> 00:12:40,610
Right.

266
00:12:40,693 --> 00:12:42,771
Are you guys familiar with mangrove trees?

267
00:12:44,300 --> 00:12:45,130
Mangroves?

268
00:12:45,213 --> 00:12:48,937
Trees with roots above or under the
water, depending on the tides, right?

269
00:12:49,020 --> 00:12:50,200
Yep, you got it.

270
00:12:50,320 --> 00:12:54,555
But the tide never rises high enough
here for the roots to be submerged.

271
00:12:54,960 --> 00:12:58,697
The Savoote Archipelago is home to the
largest mangrove trees in the world.

272
00:12:58,780 --> 00:13:01,477
These colossal giants are
the Hustle Muscle mangroves.

273
00:13:01,560 --> 00:13:03,800
The largest mangroves in the world?

274
00:13:04,180 --> 00:13:06,300
Those are some manly mangroves!

275
00:13:06,440 --> 00:13:07,616
This place is great!

276
00:13:08,380 --> 00:13:12,860
There's a total of 79 trees, and each
one serves as its own little island,

277
00:13:13,060 --> 00:13:15,377
complete with tiny towns and facilities.

278
00:13:15,460 --> 00:13:19,460
The cluster of all these trees is
known as the Sabaody Archipelago.

279
00:13:19,680 --> 00:13:23,700
Grove 44 appears the private
residence entrance, so before we land,

280
00:13:23,840 --> 00:13:26,016
we'll need to go a little further in.

281
00:13:26,140 --> 00:13:29,480
Wow, when you see them up
close, these roots are huge!

282
00:13:30,500 --> 00:13:34,897
is that a man-made bridge it
is bridges connect each one of

283
00:13:34,980 --> 00:13:41,197
the islands I see that makes
sense all right we're here this is

284
00:13:41,280 --> 00:13:42,557
a good spot to drop anchor

285
00:13:42,640 --> 00:13:44,317
welcome to Grove 41

286
00:13:44,400 --> 00:13:51,400
hey

287
00:13:54,520 --> 00:13:55,350
make sure

288
00:13:55,433 --> 00:13:58,677
you all remember the grove number
okay like Like I said earlier,

289
00:13:58,760 --> 00:14:01,557
the whole archipelago is connected
by a series of bridges so

290
00:14:01,640 --> 00:14:04,157
you won't get lost if you remember
the number you're docked at.

291
00:14:04,240 --> 00:14:06,217
There's one guy that'll still get lost.

292
00:14:06,300 --> 00:14:07,130
Yep.

293
00:14:07,380 --> 00:14:08,860
Huh? What's going on?

294
00:14:10,360 --> 00:14:11,780
Hey, what was that for?

295
00:14:18,360 --> 00:14:20,440
A bubble popped out of the ground!

296
00:14:20,760 --> 00:14:22,113
What the weird is that?

297
00:14:24,200 --> 00:14:25,030
Awesome!

298
00:14:28,720 --> 00:14:30,160
I'm riding it!

299
00:14:30,360 --> 00:14:31,889
That is one strong bubble!

300
00:14:32,300 --> 00:14:33,130
Wow!

301
00:14:36,520 --> 00:14:38,640
These soap bubbles, I'm curious.

302
00:14:39,020 --> 00:14:40,961
How exactly do they get produced?

303
00:14:41,240 --> 00:14:42,280
I got this one.

304
00:14:42,500 --> 00:14:45,397
It's a chemical reaction from
the hustle muscle mangrove roots.

305
00:14:45,480 --> 00:14:48,009
They secrete a unique
resin that causes it.

306
00:14:50,880 --> 00:14:52,740
Ugh, it's really sticky.

307
00:14:53,960 --> 00:14:55,320
Hey, stop that!

308
00:14:56,180 --> 00:14:58,357
You see, when the roots
of the trees breathe,

309
00:14:58,440 --> 00:15:01,517
the air inflates the resin as
it rises out of the ground.

310
00:15:01,600 --> 00:15:02,430
Interesting.

311
00:15:02,513 --> 00:15:05,177
I never would have thought
tree sap could flow.

312
00:15:05,260 --> 00:15:09,120
Wow, so this is all 100 % natural. Hey!

313
00:15:10,020 --> 00:15:10,850
Huh?

314
00:15:10,933 --> 00:15:12,577
Luffy, where did you get
all the way up there?

315
00:15:12,660 --> 00:15:14,477
There's an amusement park over there!

316
00:15:14,560 --> 00:15:15,390
Let's go!

317
00:15:15,473 --> 00:15:16,757
We want to ride the ferris wheel!

318
00:15:16,840 --> 00:15:17,958
Oh my gosh, really?

319
00:15:18,100 --> 00:15:19,720
Yeah, that's Sabaody Park.

320
00:15:20,420 --> 00:15:22,100
Oh, wow, I'm so jealous.

321
00:15:22,480 --> 00:15:24,977
See, I've always dreamed of
riding that ferris wheel.

322
00:15:25,060 --> 00:15:26,020
You have?

323
00:15:26,300 --> 00:15:27,397
Why don't you just write it?

324
00:15:27,480 --> 00:15:28,310
Not a chance.

325
00:15:28,393 --> 00:15:29,917
Don't you even think about it.

326
00:15:30,000 --> 00:15:32,200
Yeah, I know. Don't remind me.

327
00:15:36,260 --> 00:15:39,378
If she can't write it, does
that mean I can't either?

328
00:15:46,840 --> 00:15:50,016
So, Hachi, what's our objective
on this island anyway?

329
00:15:50,280 --> 00:15:53,737
Didn't you say something before
about getting the ship coated here?

330
00:15:53,820 --> 00:15:56,197
We'll meet up with one of the
island's coating specialists

331
00:15:56,280 --> 00:15:58,757
and have him slap a coat
of this resin on your ship.

332
00:15:58,840 --> 00:15:59,670
Huh?

333
00:15:59,753 --> 00:16:00,896
That's all it takes.

334
00:16:01,180 --> 00:16:04,817
After that, your ship will be fully
equipped for underwater travel.

335
00:16:04,900 --> 00:16:05,730
Seriously?

336
00:16:06,320 --> 00:16:08,057
Yep, the process works wonders,

337
00:16:08,140 --> 00:16:11,577
and it's the only way I know of that
humans can reach Fishman Island.

338
00:16:11,660 --> 00:16:13,557
But you don't want an amateur to do it.

339
00:16:13,640 --> 00:16:17,977
If it's not done right, the water pressure
will crush the ship and everyone on it.

340
00:16:18,060 --> 00:16:22,117
I've got one specialist that I really
trust, though, so you'll be in good hands.

341
00:16:22,200 --> 00:16:27,960
thank you for your help you really
are a good man wait good octopus

342
00:16:30,340 --> 00:16:35,837
but first in exchange for
my help promise me one thing

343
00:16:35,920 --> 00:16:40,597
sure what is it once we cross
the bridge into town there's

344
00:16:40,680 --> 00:16:44,417
a chance we might run into
the world nobles okay who

345
00:16:44,500 --> 00:16:47,676
the world nobles they're
from the Holy Land Marie Joie

346
00:16:49,320 --> 00:16:50,150
Cool!

347
00:16:50,233 --> 00:16:51,493
So what's the big deal?

348
00:16:52,920 --> 00:16:56,744
This is difficult to ask, but no
matter what happens in the town,

349
00:16:56,920 --> 00:17:00,744
you must promise that you'll do
nothing to defy the world nobles.

350
00:17:03,620 --> 00:17:05,540
I'll say it one more time.

351
00:17:07,280 --> 00:17:10,500
No matter what, you act
like you didn't see a thing!

352
00:17:13,340 --> 00:17:14,928
Everyone else went to town.

353
00:17:15,260 --> 00:17:16,997
Why didn't the two of you go with them?

354
00:17:17,080 --> 00:17:19,777
We used up a lot of cola
in that battle with Devil.

355
00:17:19,860 --> 00:17:21,036
Damn near all of it.

356
00:17:22,200 --> 00:17:24,377
It's my job to take good care of the sun.

357
00:17:24,460 --> 00:17:25,290
That's right.

358
00:17:25,373 --> 00:17:27,397
And I like helping out with
all things ship-related, too.

359
00:17:27,480 --> 00:17:29,897
Once we're done, all three
of us can head out together.

360
00:17:29,980 --> 00:17:30,837
What do you say?

361
00:17:30,920 --> 00:17:31,750
Sound good?

362
00:17:31,833 --> 00:17:32,663
Sorry.

363
00:17:32,746 --> 00:17:33,576
Thanks for the invite,

364
00:17:33,659 --> 00:17:36,357
but I can't do my shopping until
a certain someone comes back.

365
00:17:36,440 --> 00:17:37,477
Wait, what do you mean?

366
00:17:37,560 --> 00:17:38,580
Oh, you see...

367
00:17:41,740 --> 00:17:44,020
My beloved Nami was in a jam.

368
00:17:45,000 --> 00:17:45,830
Hmm.

369
00:17:45,913 --> 00:17:46,780
Now what to do?

370
00:17:47,080 --> 00:17:49,017
We have a ton of treasure on board,

371
00:17:49,100 --> 00:17:51,077
and I can't leave the ship
knowing it's unguarded.

372
00:17:51,160 --> 00:17:54,217
If only there was a valiant
knight around to keep an eye on.

373
00:17:54,300 --> 00:17:55,500
Ha-ha! That's me!

374
00:17:57,240 --> 00:17:59,497
She's got you wrapped around
her finger, doesn't she?

375
00:17:59,580 --> 00:18:01,380
I am a slave to love!

376
00:18:01,720 --> 00:18:03,955
You admitting it saves me the trouble.

377
00:18:09,740 --> 00:18:11,880
Hey! Zoro! Zoro! Wait!

378
00:18:12,880 --> 00:18:15,704
Where do you think you're
going all by yourself?

379
00:18:19,020 --> 00:18:20,020
For a walk

380
00:18:20,700 --> 00:18:22,420
Is that okay? Of course not!

381
00:18:22,860 --> 00:18:25,057
You're gonna get yourself lost, moron!

382
00:18:25,140 --> 00:18:26,437
This is an archipelago!

383
00:18:26,520 --> 00:18:27,937
We won't be able to find you!

384
00:18:28,020 --> 00:18:28,850
Screw you!

385
00:18:28,933 --> 00:18:29,763
I'm not gonna get lost!

386
00:18:29,846 --> 00:18:31,697
Only an idiot would get
turned around in a place

387
00:18:31,780 --> 00:18:34,597
like this All of these
trees have numbers on them,

388
00:18:34,680 --> 00:18:35,510
okay?

389
00:18:35,593 --> 00:18:39,221
That way it doesn't matter how bad
your sense of direction is Whoa!

390
00:18:40,100 --> 00:18:40,930
Nice job!

391
00:18:41,013 --> 00:18:45,697
You actually put some thought into this
Yeah, good call Alright then, have fun!

392
00:18:45,780 --> 00:18:48,560
Ask for directions if you get confused.

393
00:18:49,040 --> 00:18:50,628
Don't trust your instincts!

394
00:18:52,640 --> 00:18:53,740
Screw these guys.

395
00:18:53,880 --> 00:18:54,837
I'll be all right.

396
00:18:54,920 --> 00:18:57,744
I just have to remember
the number on this tree.

397
00:19:01,720 --> 00:19:03,980
And that number is one.

398
00:19:05,380 --> 00:19:07,157
What do they think I can't count?

399
00:19:07,240 --> 00:19:09,917
I have to be brained to get
lost in a place like this.

400
00:19:10,000 --> 00:19:12,294
I'm not taking any more crap from them.

401
00:19:18,640 --> 00:19:22,437
The world nobles I mentioned are
also known as the Celestial Dragons.

402
00:19:22,520 --> 00:19:24,737
They think they're so much
better than everyone else,

403
00:19:24,820 --> 00:19:27,637
they wear masks to avoid
breathing the same air as us.

404
00:19:27,720 --> 00:19:29,137
Now remember what I said.

405
00:19:29,220 --> 00:19:31,477
No matter what they do,
just stay out of their way.

406
00:19:31,560 --> 00:19:33,325
I need you to promise me that.

407
00:19:34,520 --> 00:19:35,520
Aside from that,

408
00:19:35,640 --> 00:19:39,317
there are a couple of other things you
should probably keep an eye out for.

409
00:19:39,400 --> 00:19:43,929
Remember, this is the place everyone
gathers before heading to the New World.

410
00:19:44,040 --> 00:19:47,877
In other words, like you, there are a
lot of big-name pirate crews around,

411
00:19:47,960 --> 00:19:51,057
which means Marines and bounty
hunters are out to catch them.

412
00:19:51,140 --> 00:19:55,160
Also, the law won't protect pirates
from being bought and sold here.

413
00:19:55,480 --> 00:19:57,357
Kidnapping happens all the time.

414
00:19:57,440 --> 00:19:59,240
So try not to stand out.

415
00:19:59,420 --> 00:20:01,197
If people realize how much you're worth,

416
00:20:01,280 --> 00:20:03,937
the whole island will be on you and
we'll never get the ship coated.

417
00:20:04,020 --> 00:20:06,717
And fair warning, the Marines
here aren't pushovers.

418
00:20:06,800 --> 00:20:10,857
We're right by Navy headquarters, so you
never know which powerhouses might show up.

419
00:20:10,940 --> 00:20:13,017
The bounty hunters here
are pretty ferocious, too.

420
00:20:13,100 --> 00:20:15,357
They're a lot tougher
than what you're used to.

421
00:20:15,440 --> 00:20:17,157
Oh, yeah, and one more thing.

422
00:20:17,240 --> 00:20:18,280
Oh, come on.

423
00:20:18,540 --> 00:20:20,177
We're going to be just fine.

424
00:20:20,260 --> 00:20:22,497
Kuma is no mermaid,
and I'm not a fish man.

425
00:20:22,580 --> 00:20:23,797
Not while we're here, anyway.

426
00:20:23,880 --> 00:20:25,497
Just pretend we're humans like you.

427
00:20:25,580 --> 00:20:26,410
What?

428
00:20:26,493 --> 00:20:27,323
Why would we do that?

429
00:20:27,406 --> 00:20:30,377
When traveling, it's best to
honor the local culture, Luffy.

430
00:20:30,460 --> 00:20:32,578
Let's just do what the octopus asks.

431
00:20:39,620 --> 00:20:40,450
That's it.

432
00:20:41,100 --> 00:20:41,930
Slowly.

433
00:20:47,960 --> 00:20:49,380
Look, I'm inside!

434
00:20:50,900 --> 00:20:53,160
I'll be next! How mysterious.

435
00:20:53,640 --> 00:20:57,397
I can get my whole body in here, and
none of the air is coming out either.

436
00:20:57,480 --> 00:20:59,068
You ain't seen nothing yet.

437
00:21:00,840 --> 00:21:03,428
Here, pull this thing
inside there with you.

438
00:21:05,700 --> 00:21:06,540
Like this?

439
00:21:07,140 --> 00:21:11,846
As long as you can reach the pedals, you
can drive it around all over the place.

440
00:21:14,740 --> 00:21:15,570
Ah!

441
00:21:15,653 --> 00:21:16,560
It's moving!

442
00:21:18,040 --> 00:21:19,180
Ah! Ah!

443
00:21:22,780 --> 00:21:24,700
Here it goes! Woo-hoo!

444
00:21:25,780 --> 00:21:27,600
The bubble isn't breaking.

445
00:21:29,780 --> 00:21:31,637
These bubble bites are the most convenient

446
00:21:31,720 --> 00:21:33,977
way to get around the
Zeff Odi acapella goal.

447
00:21:34,060 --> 00:21:35,397
They're affordable, too.

448
00:21:35,480 --> 00:21:39,997
They rent for 500 berries a person, but
you can own it for only 10,000 berries.

449
00:21:40,080 --> 00:21:41,117
So how about it?

450
00:21:41,200 --> 00:21:42,960
We'll just rent one. Wait!

451
00:21:43,300 --> 00:21:44,320
I got the money.

452
00:21:44,480 --> 00:21:47,220
I'm going to buy one.
Me too! Me too! Yeah.

453
00:21:47,480 --> 00:21:48,310
No, you don't.

454
00:21:48,393 --> 00:21:49,897
There's no point in buying.

455
00:21:49,980 --> 00:21:50,810
Just rent it.

456
00:21:50,893 --> 00:21:51,723
It's my money.

457
00:21:51,806 --> 00:21:52,636
I'll do what I want.

458
00:21:52,719 --> 00:21:53,549
Yeah, so that.

459
00:21:53,632 --> 00:21:55,417
Well, um, look, take my word for it.

460
00:21:55,500 --> 00:21:57,157
I'll explain everything later.

461
00:21:57,240 --> 00:21:58,416
Two rentals, please.

462
00:21:58,500 --> 00:22:00,057
I take it you're a local, then.

463
00:22:00,140 --> 00:22:00,970
Such a shame.

464
00:22:01,053 --> 00:22:01,883
Such a shame.

465
00:22:06,500 --> 00:22:07,330
Wow!

466
00:22:07,413 --> 00:22:08,243
This is fantastic.

467
00:22:08,326 --> 00:22:09,156
I love it.

468
00:22:09,239 --> 00:22:10,120
You can't stop me.

469
00:22:10,220 --> 00:22:11,417
I'm gonna buy one of these.

470
00:22:11,500 --> 00:22:12,437
Listen, Straw Hat,

471
00:22:12,520 --> 00:22:16,337
think back to when you rode that bubble
up into the sky right after we got here.

472
00:22:16,420 --> 00:22:18,017
Do you remember what happened to it?

473
00:22:18,100 --> 00:22:18,930
Uh,

474
00:22:19,013 --> 00:22:21,317
yeah, I hopped on a bubble, flew
up past the tops of the trees,

475
00:22:21,400 --> 00:22:24,597
and tried to jump around to
other ones to go even higher.

476
00:22:24,680 --> 00:22:27,857
But out of nowhere, all the
bubbles around me started popping.

477
00:22:27,940 --> 00:22:30,234
And the one I was riding on popped too.

478
00:22:31,280 --> 00:22:33,057
And then I fell down.

479
00:22:33,140 --> 00:22:36,797
That happened because you left the Sabo
Odi Archipelago's unique atmosphere.

480
00:22:36,880 --> 00:22:42,160
This area has a distinct climate specifically
suited to the Hustle Muscle mangroves.

481
00:22:42,360 --> 00:22:45,817
Once you leave that climate, the
resin in the bubble starts to change.

482
00:22:45,900 --> 00:22:47,665
Not long after that, they pop.

483
00:22:48,240 --> 00:22:49,070
Really?

484
00:22:49,153 --> 00:22:50,937
That means someone would
only be able to ride

485
00:22:51,020 --> 00:22:53,197
one of these bubbles if
they stayed in this area,

486
00:22:53,280 --> 00:22:54,180
correct? Yeah.

487
00:22:54,640 --> 00:22:55,620
See, you get it.

488
00:22:55,800 --> 00:22:59,637
People who come here for the first time
are always eager to buy a bubble bike.

489
00:22:59,720 --> 00:23:01,917
Since they only work here, it's a rip-off.

490
00:23:02,000 --> 00:23:04,157
Just renting one is all you really need.

491
00:23:04,240 --> 00:23:05,070
I don't care!

492
00:23:05,160 --> 00:23:06,219
I want to buy one!

493
00:23:06,880 --> 00:23:09,377
All I heard was blub,
blub, blub, bubble bite.

494
00:23:09,460 --> 00:23:11,537
How many ways do we have
to spell it out for you?

495
00:23:11,620 --> 00:23:13,897
Once you leave this island, the
bubbles aren't strong enough.

496
00:23:13,980 --> 00:23:14,810
They just pop.

497
00:23:14,980 --> 00:23:16,417
It's quite the mystery, isn't it?

498
00:23:16,500 --> 00:23:17,517
Whoa, what the hell?

499
00:23:17,600 --> 00:23:18,817
They're mystery bubbles?

500
00:23:18,900 --> 00:23:21,240
Why didn't you say so before? We did.

501
00:23:21,360 --> 00:23:22,517
Why don't you ever listen?

502
00:23:22,600 --> 00:23:26,017
Oh, you can use bubble bites on
Fishman Island, too, if you like.

503
00:23:26,100 --> 00:23:28,097
The ocean floor has the
same kind of bubbles.

504
00:23:28,180 --> 00:23:29,010
You'll love it.

505
00:23:29,093 --> 00:23:31,620
Ooh, I can't wait to
get to Fishman Island.

506
00:23:31,800 --> 00:23:33,271
It's going to be awesome.

507
00:23:33,420 --> 00:23:35,577
In that case, you should
meet the mermaid princess.

508
00:23:35,660 --> 00:23:37,760
So graceful, so beautiful.

509
00:23:38,200 --> 00:23:41,141
Sometimes it's all you can
do not to stare at her.

510
00:23:41,260 --> 00:23:42,840
I look forward to it.

511
00:23:43,020 --> 00:23:45,777
I have an excellent eye
for appreciating beauty.

512
00:23:45,860 --> 00:23:49,154
Though being a skeleton, I
don't actually have any eyes.

513
00:23:50,840 --> 00:23:51,940
Do you get it?

514
00:23:52,180 --> 00:23:54,700
That stuff looks yummy! It's a grammon.

515
00:23:55,140 --> 00:23:56,680
A gram-line steamed buns.

516
00:23:56,980 --> 00:23:58,457
They're called grammon for short.

517
00:23:58,540 --> 00:23:59,775
Care to try a sample?

518
00:24:03,400 --> 00:24:07,106
As you can see, it's got Grand
Line First Half written into it.

519
00:24:07,380 --> 00:24:10,117
They're meant to be a
souvenir to return home with.

520
00:24:10,200 --> 00:24:11,677
Shelf life's three months.

521
00:24:11,760 --> 00:24:13,557
Plenty of time to make it back with them.

522
00:24:13,640 --> 00:24:14,470
Delicious!

523
00:24:16,680 --> 00:24:19,377
Would it be all right if I
sampled another box or two?

524
00:24:19,460 --> 00:24:20,931
Aren't you gonna buy any?

525
00:24:25,960 --> 00:24:26,880
Grove 35.

526
00:24:27,460 --> 00:24:29,597
There seem to be a lot
of hotels around here.

527
00:24:29,680 --> 00:24:31,797
Those are the living
quarters of the sailors who

528
00:24:31,880 --> 00:24:34,077
are waiting for permission
to pass through Marijua.

529
00:24:34,160 --> 00:24:36,677
Building all these hotels
is easier than you'd think.

530
00:24:36,760 --> 00:24:37,590
See?

531
00:24:37,673 --> 00:24:41,319
They simply coat the giant soap
bubbles with a metal alloy and Fall!

532
00:24:41,780 --> 00:24:42,837
Instant foundation.

533
00:24:42,920 --> 00:24:44,837
That's how all the round
buildings are made.

534
00:24:44,920 --> 00:24:45,750
Wow.

535
00:24:46,220 --> 00:24:47,050
Robin!

536
00:24:47,280 --> 00:24:49,157
Amal, I bet they have all sorts of stuff.

537
00:24:49,240 --> 00:24:50,097
Let's check it out.

538
00:24:50,180 --> 00:24:51,760
Stop by any time!

539
00:24:53,200 --> 00:24:54,030
Cratchaco!

540
00:24:54,113 --> 00:24:57,080
And crackers, too! A
keychain! And a pudding!

541
00:24:57,400 --> 00:24:59,117
Hold on to those precious memories!

542
00:24:59,200 --> 00:25:00,577
You guys bought a lot of stuff.

543
00:25:00,660 --> 00:25:02,917
It'll be tough to carry
all that junk around.

544
00:25:03,000 --> 00:25:05,037
Go have him bubble pack it up for you.

545
00:25:05,120 --> 00:25:06,355
What's a bubble pack?

546
00:25:08,600 --> 00:25:09,953
Awesome, it's so light!

547
00:25:10,080 --> 00:25:13,021
Carrying around stuff in
this place is super easy.

548
00:25:16,020 --> 00:25:17,637
Hey, where are Robin and Nami?

549
00:25:17,720 --> 00:25:18,717
Don't worry about them.

550
00:25:18,800 --> 00:25:20,657
They went to the shopping
mall on Grove 30.

551
00:25:20,740 --> 00:25:23,437
They said that they wanted to leave
the coating of the ship to us.

552
00:25:23,520 --> 00:25:24,350
Oh, yeah?

553
00:25:24,680 --> 00:25:26,357
Right, leave it to us then.

554
00:25:26,440 --> 00:25:28,017
So where are we headed next, Hachi?

555
00:25:28,100 --> 00:25:29,740
We're going to Grove 31.

556
00:25:30,240 --> 00:25:34,064
Even by bike, it's a long trip,
so we should probably get moving.

557
00:25:36,020 --> 00:25:38,140
I wonder why Kuma didn't join us.

558
00:25:38,240 --> 00:25:39,600
We invited her. Yeah.

559
00:25:39,880 --> 00:25:43,337
She's been sort of nervous and quiet
ever since we got here, hasn't she?

560
00:25:43,420 --> 00:25:46,302
Something's bothering her,
but I don't know what.

561
00:25:48,260 --> 00:25:49,597
Perhaps it's Sabo O .D.

562
00:25:49,680 --> 00:25:50,510
itself.

563
00:25:50,593 --> 00:25:53,064
There could be a bad
history tied to the island.

564
00:25:53,200 --> 00:25:55,000
A bad history, huh?

565
00:26:02,360 --> 00:26:03,190
Yeah!

566
00:26:03,400 --> 00:26:04,230
I'm winning!

567
00:26:04,313 --> 00:26:05,143
I'm winning!

568
00:26:05,226 --> 00:26:06,056
I'm winning!

569
00:26:06,139 --> 00:26:07,520
Don't get so cocky!

570
00:26:07,720 --> 00:26:11,140
We've still got a long way
to go! Yeah! Keep it up!

571
00:26:11,300 --> 00:26:12,537
You can do it, Hanson!

572
00:26:12,620 --> 00:26:14,197
What the heck is happening, you guys?

573
00:26:14,280 --> 00:26:16,197
Why did this turn into some kind of race?

574
00:26:16,280 --> 00:26:17,110
Yeah!

575
00:26:17,193 --> 00:26:18,023
Yeah!

576
00:26:18,160 --> 00:26:18,990
Yeah! Yeah!

577
00:26:19,073 --> 00:26:21,220
Yeah! Yeah! Yeah! Yeah! Yeah!

578
00:26:21,780 --> 00:26:22,680
Yeah! Yeah!

579
00:26:35,860 --> 00:26:38,200
Hey, what's all I yelling about?

580
00:26:40,300 --> 00:26:43,760
Anybody, please, get me
out of this damn thing!

581
00:26:45,100 --> 00:26:46,340
Bring me something!

582
00:26:46,740 --> 00:26:48,540
Somebody bring me a damn tool!

583
00:26:48,840 --> 00:26:52,420
An axe, a saw, something
to get this thing off me!

584
00:26:52,680 --> 00:26:55,300
All I want is to go back home.

585
00:26:55,540 --> 00:26:57,187
I don't want to hurt anybody

586
00:27:05,700 --> 00:27:07,160
I give up.

587
00:27:07,340 --> 00:27:10,317
I don't want to go to the
new world anymore, please.

588
00:27:10,400 --> 00:27:13,840
I've got a wife and kid back
home I'm begging you here.

589
00:27:14,220 --> 00:27:15,600
Somebody help me

590
00:27:16,320 --> 00:27:17,580
My little boy.

591
00:27:17,740 --> 00:27:19,620
I left when he was just a baby.

592
00:27:19,840 --> 00:27:22,100
He doesn't even know what I look like

593
00:27:22,680 --> 00:27:29,097
Help me please who's that I want
to go home that's all that matters

594
00:27:29,180 --> 00:27:33,217
now I won't hurt you let's stay
Out of this he's probably just some

595
00:27:33,300 --> 00:27:36,957
pirate who was caught by kidnappers
and sold into slavery His owner

596
00:27:37,040 --> 00:27:40,922
must have brought him to this
island and then he made a run for it

597
00:27:41,140 --> 00:27:44,611
But he must know what happens
to slaves who try to get away

598
00:27:52,680 --> 00:27:54,980
What's that sound? Why is it ticking?

599
00:27:56,460 --> 00:27:57,660
This collar!

600
00:27:58,020 --> 00:28:03,340
If I could only get this thing
off my neck! Stop it! Please!

601
00:28:03,680 --> 00:28:06,900
Stop ticking! Damn it! Damn it!

602
00:28:07,300 --> 00:28:08,620
Get off me!

603
00:28:26,940 --> 00:28:27,980
Help me.

604
00:28:31,440 --> 00:28:34,857
Every slave has one of those metal
collars put around their neck.

605
00:28:34,940 --> 00:28:39,116
And if they try to take it off or
run from their master, it'll explode.

606
00:28:41,300 --> 00:28:43,980
Just let me go home to my family.

607
00:28:44,760 --> 00:28:48,400
I don't want to be a pirate
in the new world anymore.

608
00:28:53,580 --> 00:28:54,410
Ah!

609
00:28:54,493 --> 00:28:56,100
It's a slave that tried to escape!

610
00:28:56,980 --> 00:28:59,000
Everybody, stay back! Ignore him!

611
00:28:59,180 --> 00:29:00,917
I can't believe what just happened.

612
00:29:01,000 --> 00:29:01,830
We have to help!

613
00:29:01,913 --> 00:29:04,897
Idiot, you guys promised not to get
involved no matter what, remember?

614
00:29:04,980 --> 00:29:05,810
Ah!

615
00:29:05,893 --> 00:29:07,217
What's with this crazy place?

616
00:29:07,300 --> 00:29:08,757
What are we gonna do, Hachi?

617
00:29:08,840 --> 00:29:11,781
And the Celestial Dragons
will be here any minute!

618
00:29:12,400 --> 00:29:13,277
It's all right.

619
00:29:13,360 --> 00:29:14,800
Just stay calm, Kuma.

620
00:29:15,220 --> 00:29:19,220
Listen, Straw Hat, you need to get
off that bubble bike. What for?

621
00:29:19,460 --> 00:29:20,580
Hurry up and do it!

622
00:29:21,380 --> 00:29:22,210
Fine.

623
00:29:22,400 --> 00:29:23,440
Just this once.

624
00:29:31,060 --> 00:29:31,920
They're here.

625
00:29:36,760 --> 00:29:41,040
That's not a dragon. Bow down! But why?

626
00:29:41,380 --> 00:29:43,717
No matter what happens,
don't look them in the eye.

627
00:29:43,800 --> 00:29:44,937
Same goes for you guys.

628
00:29:45,020 --> 00:29:45,850
Right.

629
00:29:46,860 --> 00:29:48,077
Saru, come now.

630
00:29:48,160 --> 00:29:49,320
Don't be vulgar.

631
00:29:49,980 --> 00:29:51,860
Those are dragons. Yeah.

632
00:30:14,760 --> 00:30:16,120
Oh, look, Father.

633
00:30:16,560 --> 00:30:18,597
Another one of our slaves has broken down.

634
00:30:18,680 --> 00:30:22,137
Did you give it its daily sedative
like you were supposed to?

635
00:30:22,220 --> 00:30:23,300
Of course I did.

636
00:30:23,520 --> 00:30:26,344
But it seems it had no
effect on this poor fool.

637
00:30:27,940 --> 00:30:29,800
I don't even want it anymore.

638
00:30:30,000 --> 00:30:31,588
Would you buy me a new one?

639
00:30:31,880 --> 00:30:34,477
Honestly, you're terrible
at taking care of them.

640
00:30:34,560 --> 00:30:38,757
You're decimating my precious ship
captain collection one pirate at a time.

641
00:30:38,840 --> 00:30:42,200
It was useless to begin
with. Family. Children.

642
00:30:42,920 --> 00:30:43,880
Stop crying.

643
00:30:44,540 --> 00:30:45,370
Pathetic.

644
00:30:45,453 --> 00:30:49,317
You're nothing but a lowly human slave.

645
00:30:49,400 --> 00:30:52,097
She can't even move.

646
00:30:52,180 --> 00:30:57,500
You make me want to vomit!

647
00:31:01,700 --> 00:31:03,777
Shut down, control yourself.

648
00:31:03,860 --> 00:31:06,897
I think I'd like a
giant for my next slave.

649
00:31:06,980 --> 00:31:09,497
Perhaps something smaller,
like a human child.

650
00:31:09,580 --> 00:31:11,720
I detest the weak ones.

651
00:31:12,740 --> 00:31:15,505
Whatever you're thinking,
don't think about it?

652
00:31:15,640 --> 00:31:16,500
The Marines!

653
00:31:20,320 --> 00:31:22,967
We need to get the hell
away from here, fast!

654
00:31:30,060 --> 00:31:31,557
Would you care for some tea?

655
00:31:31,640 --> 00:31:32,993
It'll calm your nerves.

656
00:31:33,840 --> 00:31:34,670
Uh-uh.

657
00:31:34,753 --> 00:31:36,320
I feel terrible. Thanks, though.

658
00:31:36,720 --> 00:31:38,880
You think he's gonna be all right?

659
00:31:39,040 --> 00:31:42,157
Maybe so, but if he lives,
he'll go to prison for piracy.

660
00:31:42,240 --> 00:31:43,358
I don't understand.

661
00:31:43,580 --> 00:31:46,417
An old man and a woman are no
match for a pirate like that.

662
00:31:46,500 --> 00:31:47,597
What's going on here?

663
00:31:47,680 --> 00:31:49,739
If anyone hurts a celestial dragon,

664
00:31:49,900 --> 00:31:51,757
Navy Headquarters sends an admiral and a

665
00:31:51,840 --> 00:31:54,487
fleet of battleships to
handle the situation.

666
00:31:56,040 --> 00:31:56,917
An admiral?

667
00:31:57,000 --> 00:31:58,260
You mean Aokiji?

668
00:31:58,380 --> 00:32:00,477
It could be him or Aka 'inu or Kizaru.

669
00:32:00,560 --> 00:32:02,317
No telling which one of them will show up.

670
00:32:02,400 --> 00:32:04,047
Remember, we're right by HQ.

671
00:32:04,320 --> 00:32:06,637
What makes those celestial
dragons so special?

672
00:32:06,720 --> 00:32:10,597
The dragons are from the bloodline of
the creators of the world government.

673
00:32:10,680 --> 00:32:11,720
Are you serious?

674
00:32:12,380 --> 00:32:15,697
800 years ago a group of 20
kings came together to create

675
00:32:15,780 --> 00:32:18,357
the organization that's now
known as the world government?

676
00:32:18,440 --> 00:32:20,797
The Celestial Dragons
are their descendants

677
00:32:20,880 --> 00:32:24,197
as the years go by
generation after generation!

678
00:32:24,280 --> 00:32:26,868
They grow more and more
reckless with power!

679
00:32:27,980 --> 00:32:29,000
Celestial dragons
